"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"}},{"id":"401892659000000690","scoringPlay":false,"scoreValue":0,"awayScore":0,"homeScore":0,"text":"Peyton Krebs faceoff won against Sean Monahan","type":{"id":"502","text":"Face Off","abbreviation":"faceoff"},"clock":{"displayValue":"1:05"},"period":{"number":1,"displayValue":"1st"},"team":{"id":"2"},"participants":[{"athlete":{"id":"4565238","displayName":"Peyton Krebs","shortName":"P. Krebs"},"type":"face-off-winner"},{"athlete":{"id":"3041996","displayName":"Sean Monahan","shortName":"S. Monahan"}}]}],"gameInfo":{"venue":{"id":"1848","fullName":"KeyBank Center","address":{"city":"Buffalo","state":"NY","country":"USA"},"grass":false,"images":[{"href":"https://a.espncdn.com/i/venues/nhl/day/1848.jpg","width":2000,"height":1125,"alt":"","rel":["full","day"]}]},"attendance":19070,"officials":[{"fullName":"Garrett Rank","displayName":"Garrett Rank","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"James Tobias","displayName":"James Tobias","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Michael Markovic","displayName":"Michael Markovic","position":{"name":"Referee","displayName":"Referee","id":"24"},"order":0},{"fullName":"Brandon Grillo","displayName":"Brandon Grillo","position":{"name":"Linesman","displayName":"Linesman","id":"25"},"order":0}]},"article":{"headline":"Josh Norris scores twice in the Sabres' 5-2 victory over the Blue Jackets","description":"— Josh Norris scored twice, defenseman Owen Power had three assists and the Buffalo Sabres beat the Columbus Blue Jackets 5-2 on Friday night.","story":"BUFFALO, N.Y. -- — <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4233627/josh-norris\">Josh Norris</a> scored twice, defenseman <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4781556/owen-power\">Owen Power</a> had three assists and the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/buf/buffalo-sabres\">Buffalo Sabres</a> beat the <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/team/_/name/cbj/columbus-blue-jackets\">Columbus Blue Jackets</a> 5-2 on Friday night.\n\n\r\n              Norris ended a six-game goals drought to help Buffalo win for the fourth time in five games.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4697389/jack-quinn\">Jack Quinn</a>, <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4294163/rasmus-dahlin\">Rasmus Dahlin</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4874870/josh-doan\">Josh Doan</a> also scored, and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4233889/ukko-pekka-luukkonen\">Ukko-Pekka Luukkonen</a> made 24 saves.\n\n\r\n              <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4781553/kent-johnson\">Kent Johnson</a> and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3899972/zach-werenski\">Zach Werenski</a> scored for Columbus, and <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/4894366/jet-greaves\">Jet Greaves</a> made 32 saves. The Blue Jackets have lost three straight road games.\n\n\r\n              Quinn opened the scoring at 6:50 of the first period with his ninth of the season, and Johnson tied it with 4:00 left in the period with his eighth. Norris made it 2-1 with 1:50 to go in the first with his first goal since Oct. 17.\n\n\r\n              Dahlin made it 3-1 with a one-timer 4:30 into the second period. Norris’ second goal at 9:46 made it 4-1. Doan made it 5-1 1:07 later.\n\n\r\n              Werenski's power-play goal with 1:39 left in the third made it 5-2. \n\n\r\n              Blue Jackets forward <a href=\"http://www.espn.com/nhl/player/_/id/3041996/sean-monahan\">Sean Monahan</a> left the second period because of a lower-body injury and did not return. He blocked Dahlin's shot during his last shift.\n\n\r\n              <hl2>Up next</hl2>\r\n              Blue Jackets: Host Florida on Tuesday night.\n\n\r\n              Sabres: Host Vegas on Sunday.\n\n\r\n              ------\n\n\r\n              \r\n                <a href=\"https://apnews.com/hub/nhl\">See AP’s full NHL coverage here</a>","published":"2026-11-07T02:57:36Z"}}